    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d231-a1">

                <pb facs="0377" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg283"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 336.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Flourens to Mr.
                            McLane</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-01-06"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 6,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: By a note of the 13th of December last, you
                    were pleased to express the desire of obtaining for the volunteer “Gate City
                    Guards” of Atlanta, the authorization to wear their uniforms, and to carry their
                    arms during their stay in France, which they propose to visit in the summer of
                    1887.</p>
                <p>After having taken the advice of the ministers of the interior and of war, I am
                    happy to advise you that the application of this organization meets with no
                    objection on the part of the Government of the Republic. I shall be obliged to
                    you to kindly inform me, when the time comes, of the exact elate of the arrival
                    of the “Gate City Guards” of Atlanta.</p>
                <p>Please receive, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Flourens.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
